# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Abou Sobhi — configuration
#
# Copy to .env.local for development, or set these in your host's dashboard.
# The app runs with none of them set, on documented development defaults, so
# `npm run dev` works out of the box. Both of the first two are REQUIRED before
# the shop goes live — the admin panel shows a warning banner until they are.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The one password the staff type to reach the admin panel.
# Development default: "abousobhi".
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Signs the staff session cookie. Any long random string; changing it signs
# everyone out. Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
SESSION_SECRET=

# Where the SQLite database file lives. Defaults to ./data/abou-sobhi.db.
# On a host with a mounted volume, point this at the volume:
#   DATABASE_PATH=/data/abou-sobhi.db
DATABASE_PATH=

# Everything else — store name, phone, WhatsApp, opening hours, the dollar
# rate, delivery zones and every price — is edited from the admin panel and
# stored in the database. There is nothing else to configure in a file.
